Dragnet: the names are changed on the way to the screen
=======================================================

The Hermes panel lists this machine's own library, and that library is written about its owner by name.
The shipped skills are clean, but the panel also reads the local library, and a screenshot of the app
therefore carried a household with it — in the card titles, in the descriptions, in the text the search
matches against, and behind the "Read instructions" button, where the file used to arrive unredacted.

This does not rewrite anything on disk. It changes what the page shows: the owner becomes "the user",
everybody else becomes "someone". The handle in the title bar stays, because it is on the tin.

`Max` is deliberately not in the list. It is a first name and it is also `Max: 250` and `Max width: 60`,
and since the reader redacts file bodies, mapping it turns working instructions into nonsense.

